# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true`, so a clone rewrites every checked-out file to
# CRLF. A shell script that arrives that way does not run: bash reads the carriage return as part of
# the last word on the line. A hook that dies mid-parse exits 2, and exit 2 on a `Stop` hook means
# block, so the plugin would hand the agent a syntax error every turn instead of a score.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree on every platform, whatever the clone is configured to do.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh  text eol=lf
*.awk text eol=lf
